  "description": "LUYDUF crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C102 H143 Gd4 N6 O17 S10 3+,3(N1 O3 1-),2(C3 H7 N1 O1),3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2B (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.601-5.174 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.69-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C102H143Gd4N6O17S10·3(NO3)·2(dmf)·3(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
